Package: pollimetry
Type: Package
Title: Estimate Pollinator Body Size and Co-Varying Ecological Traits
Version: 1.1.1
Authors@R: c(person("Liam","Kendall", email = "liam.k.kendall@gmail.com",role=c("aut","cre")),
           person("Ignasi","Bartomeus", email = "nacho.bartomeus@gmail.com",role="aut"))
Maintainer: Liam Kendall <liam.k.kendall@gmail.com>
Description: Tools to estimate pollinator body size and co-varying traits. This package contains
           Bayesian predictive models of pollinator body size (for bees and hoverflies) and
           bee foraging range, as well as preexisting predictive models for pollinator body size
           (currently implemented for ants, bees, butterflies, flies, moths and wasps), bee tongue
           length, foraging range, total field nectar loads and wing loading. An additional GitHub
           repository <https://github.com/liamkendall/pollimetrydata> provides model objects to use
           the bodysize and foraging.range functions internally. The Bayesian models are described in Kendall
           et al. (2019) <doi:10.1002/ece3.4835> & Kendall et al. (2022) <doi:10.1002/ecy.3809>.
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: stats, utils, lifecycle, brms (>= 2.16.1)
Suggests: pollimetrydata
License: GPL (>= 2)
LazyData: true
Encoding: UTF-8
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
URL: https://github.com/liamkendall/pollimetry
BugReports: https://github.com/liamkendall/pollimetry/issues
